# Deliberately short.
#
# config.yaml, docs/feed.json, docs/config.json and triage.json are all MEANT to
# be committed in your own instance: GitHub Actions needs config.yaml to rebuild
# the feed, GitHub Pages needs the JSON files to serve the app, and triage.json
# in the repo is how the app syncs your decisions across devices. Ignoring them
# is what breaks the whole loop.
#
# The one thing that must never be committed is a token — keep NCBI_API_KEY in
# your environment or a repo secret, and the GitHub PAT only in the browser.

.env
.env.*

# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
venv/
*.egg-info/

# Editors and OS
.DS_Store
.idea/
.vscode/
